"""Freeze reviewed batch03 interpretations, separate from the screening scores."""
import csv,json
from pathlib import Path
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
Q=list(csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(newline='',encoding='utf-8')))
# verdict, period, epoch, depth, deciding evidence, limitations, next check
V={
 'H021':('PLAUSIBLE','','','','s38 has a complete shallow flat-bottomed raw dip near BTJD 2337.43. s65 captures a narrow ingress near 3082.66 before a long gap and is an additional observing occasion without a center. s100 has a deeper irregular dip on a strongly evolving baseline near 4088.3–4088.5. The rough 20/47-cycle ~37.25–37.26 d clock is conditional on all three being the same eclipse kind and source. Independent s38 TESSCut aperture recovers ~12.6 ppt, but its difference centroid is 0.63 pixel from target toward a G 11.09 star 35.7 arcsec away that could supply the signal; s100 difference centroid is instead 0.085 pixel from target.','Recurring eclipse and target attribution remain insecure; the two difference positions do not establish a shared source. No precision period, epoch, or depth assigned.','Obtain resolved/difference-image photometry for a complete future event and compare the nearby bright star.'),
 'H022':('CONFIRMED','32.023','1548.760','150','Two eclipse kinds recur in raw SAP. Deeper complete events in s9/s36/s89/s100 fit a 32.02305 d clock over 79 cycles; shallower events in s9/s36/s62/s89 independently fit 32.02299 d. Gaia SB1 has P=32.02240 ± 0.00400 d and the fitted kinds fall within ~0.004 phase of opposite edge-on conjunctions. s62 has a fully sampled secondary trough at predicted BTJD 3005.80; its first eclipse starts in the flat bottom at sector entry. An independent TESSCut s36 aperture recovers ~139.5 ppt; difference centroid is 0.04 pixel from target and no individual Gaia neighbor within 60 arcsec is flux-capable under the approximate G-band bound.','Period and epoch are rounded local trapezoid estimates, not calibrated errors. s62 first event is partial; TESSCut and SAP share photons. Neighbor bound is bandpass and aperture dependent.','Obtain independent future photometry and a precision ephemeris for publication.'),
 'H023':('PROBABLE','44.872','1699.987','20','Deeper eclipses in s14/s55/s82 have fitted centers BTJD 1699.9899, 2821.7915, 3539.7622 and a 41-cycle 44.87246 d clock with fitted epoch/intercept 1699.9871; shallower events in s15/s82 give ~44.8718 d. Their ~15.94 d separation agrees with the ~15.92 d Gaia eccentric-orbit conjunction separation. Independent TESSCut s55 aperture recovers ~16.7 ppt and difference centroid is 0.07 pixel from target.','The photometric period is 2.85 marginal Gaia period errors shorter than 45.00439 d, with ~2.9 d absolute phase drift at s14; orbital covariance is unavailable. Gaia neighbors at 13.5 and 19.4 arcsec are flux-capable and close enough to limit attribution despite the centroid favoring target. TESSCut shares photons with SAP; no calibrated period error.','Deblend the close neighbors with high-resolution or simultaneous pixel photometry and test a new eclipse against both clocks.'),
 'H024':('REFUTED','','','','The sole retained s71 dip at BTJD 3239.29 is the end of a declining baseline before a sector gap; the post-gap segment begins at a lower state and then rises. s6/s33/s45/s87 show large, evolving broad trends and brightenings rather than a matched isolated eclipse.','Refutation is of the selected s71 eclipse interpretation; the source of broad variability is not established. Current TESSCut sector inventory adds s44 and an anomalous 1751 entry beyond cached files, neither a needed repeat for this artifact conclusion.','Study the broad variability with a stable aperture if scientifically useful.'),
 'H025':('REFUTED','','','','Thirty raw SAP sectors show persistent broad multi-day modulation and many gap offsets. Retained s63/s66/s87/s88 dip windows fall on changing slopes or low states, and bright flags mark the same undulations; no stable isolated eclipse kind recurs at the Gaia conjunctions.','The selected eclipse interpretation is refuted by its broad evolving morphology; this does not exclude an unobserved eclipse elsewhere.','Characterize the non-eclipse variability separately if pursued.'),
 'H026':('REFUTED','','','','The s66 retained dip at BTJD 3111.06 is a low segment bounded by large discontinuities and a gap, not a resolved ingress and egress. s39/s93/s103/s104 exhibit much larger broad trends and ramp/reset behavior; s103 brightening is part of that variation.','Selected dip is a gap/baseline artifact in this reduction; physical source of broader variation is unassigned. Current sector inventory contains exactly the six cached sectors.','Use stable independent photometry to study broad variation if desired.'),
 'H027':('CONFIRMED','41.94565','1676.361','14','Four narrow V-shaped raw eclipses in s13/s27/s67/s94 have independent fitted centers BTJD 1676.36097, 2053.87179, 3144.45939, 3857.53608. Integer cycles 0/9/35/52 give 41.94565 d and later timing residuals under 0.002 d. Nearby 5–14 first-interval assignments disagree by days except 9; the 20.9728 d half-period predicts a fully sampled s94 event at 3878.51, where no comparable dip occurs. Gaia P=41.96173 ± 0.02910 d and predicted conjunction at s13 differs by 0.10 d. Independent s67 TESSCut aperture recovers ~10.3 ppt; difference centroid lies 0.16 pixel from target, with capable Gaia neighbors 40–43 arcsec away at distinct WCS positions.','Local triangular-model centers/depths have no calibrated error. Gaia orbital covariance is unavailable; quoted geometry is approximate. Pixel reduction shares photons with SAP, and neighbor flux ratios use approximate G band. The broad s94 feature near 3874.6 is not assigned to this narrow eclipse kind.','Observe another complete narrow eclipse with resolved photometry and fit a precision clock.'),
 'H028':('REFUTED','','','','The only retained s59 dip at BTJD 2924.73 starts exactly at the post-gap low-flux recovery and relaxes monotonically over ~1 d; it has no ingress. Full 16-sector raw SAP context contains gap recoveries and low-amplitude baseline evolution, not a matching isolated eclipse.','Refutes this selected event as an eclipse; does not prove no other eclipse exists. Current sector inventory also lists s47, absent from cached QLP files, but cannot rescue the positive gap-recovery feature.','Inspect a stable future conjunction if a separate signal is found.'),
 'H029':('REFUTED','','','','The s40 selected depression spans a changing multi-day low state and ends in a sharp recovery near BTJD 2415; another broad low/recovery near 2400 and surrounding sectors show evolving variability rather than a stable eclipse morphology. The selected brightening marks that recovery.','The selected eclipse interpretation is refuted; the broad variability has no assigned mechanism. Current sector inventory lists s53 beyond the cached set, without changing the s40 morphology.','Study the broad variability in an independent light curve if useful.'),
 'H030':('REFUTED','','','','s13 has several 3–4 d undulations, with broad troughs around 1670.85 and 1674.93; s39/s66/s93/s103 show further changing multi-day modulation, while s100–s102 contain ramps and large steps. The retained dips do not form an isolated stable eclipse kind on a 40 d clock.','Selected eclipse interpretation is refuted by evolving morphology; it does not rule out a separate hidden eclipse or identify the variability mechanism.','Analyze the multi-day variability separately if pursued.'),
}
fields=['sample_id','tic','sample_stratum','physical_verdict','full_review_completion','novelty_status','period_days','period_error_days','primary_epoch_btjd','depth_ppt','limitations','next_check','report']
rows=[]
for q in Q:
 sid=q['sample_id'];tic=q['tic'];v,p,e,d,evidence,limits,nextcheck=V[sid]
 src=json.loads((B/tic/'raw-inspection.json').read_text());sectors=[s['sector'] for s in src['sectors'] if 'path' in s]
 text=(f'# {sid} — TIC {tic}\n\nPhysical verdict: **{v}**. Bounded review: **COMPLETE**. Catalogue novelty: **UNKNOWN**; four scoped VizieR gates were unavailable after a positive-control timeout. A primary-table nonmatch is not novelty clearance.\n\n'
       f'Gaia DR3 source {q["gaia_dr3"]}, SB1 period {float(q["gaia_period_days"]):.5f} d. Frozen stratum `{q["sample_stratum"]}`; sample ID is not a new-system acceptance. Quality-zero raw SAP sectors inspected: {", ".join(map(str,sectors))}.\n\n'
       f'## Deciding evidence\n\n{evidence}\n\n## Limits and next check\n\n{limits} {nextcheck}\n\n'
       f'## Reproducibility\n\n`raw-inspection.json` verifies original bulk-result and FITS SHA-256 values and tabulates representative screening windows. `raw-windows.png` shows these raw windows; `orbit-context.json` and `.png` show full cached-sector SAP and Gaia edge-on conjunction predictions. Screening/conjunction times are not measured event centers. The frozen [source packet](../../source-packets/{tic}/sources.json), [central novelty evidence](../../shared-catalogues/target-evidence.json), batch scripts and SHA256SUMS.json preserve receipts.\n')
 if sid in ('H022','H023'):
  text+='\n`local-fits.json` and `event-clock.json` preserve fitted centers, distinct eclipse kinds, conditional integer cycles, Gaia comparison and model limitations. [Independent pixel attribution](../helper-source-attribution.json) has Gaia/WCS neighbor positions, aperture extraction and difference image; the separate `lead-pixels` cutouts are retained with hashes.\n'
 if sid=='H021':
  text+='\n[Independent helper audit](../helper-audit.md), [source attribution](../helper-source-attribution.json), and the s100 pixel `../helper-pixels/299187993-s100/analysis.json` document the two different difference positions and partial s65 occasion.\n'
 if sid=='H027':
  text+='\n[Independent helper audit](../helper-audit.md), [source attribution](../helper-source-attribution.json), `../helper-timing.json`, and helper pixel receipts document the event timing, aliases and WCS assessment.\n'
 if sid=='H027':text+='\nThe [half-period null](../helper-half-alias.json) records actual quality-zero cadence coverage and baseline around BTJD 3878.51. [Orbital calculation](../helper-orbit.json) uses marginal errors only; it is not a covariance-aware significance test.\n'
 if sid=='H022':text+='\nThe result epoch 1548.760 is the fitted multi-event clock intercept; the individual s9 center is 1548.745. The [s62 check](../helper-s62-check.json) resolves the apparent later flag as egress rather than a shifted center. The deeper kind is provisionally labeled primary; component identity is not determined.\n'
 if tic in ('445948155','42217912','402951606','396798138'):text+='\n`sector-availability.raw` and `../sector-availability.json` record the current TESSCut sector inventory and response hash.\n'
 (B/tic/'REPORT.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
 rows.append(dict(sample_id=sid,tic=tic,sample_stratum=q['sample_stratum'],physical_verdict=v,full_review_completion='COMPLETE',novelty_status='UNKNOWN',period_days=p,period_error_days='',primary_epoch_btjd=e,depth_ppt=d,limitations=limits,next_check=nextcheck,report=str((B/tic/'REPORT.md').resolve())))
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8') as f:
 writer=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);writer.writeheader();writer.writerows(rows)
print({v:sum(x['physical_verdict']==v for x in rows) for v in sorted({x['physical_verdict'] for x in rows})})
